# SABOTAGE: CF-17(b) (ADR-048 §6 / ruling UXD-18) — THE REPLAY BILLS FOR THE FOLD IT CLAIMS
# TO REUSE. `reuse_fold!/5`'s `:advance` gains the two token counters `apply_fold!/4`
# already charged at checkpoint 1, so every replay of a crashed folding turn charges the
# tenant a SECOND time for a fold that was derived exactly once. Nothing else moves: the
# `meta.replayed` stamp is still written, the ledger still holds exactly one entry per turn
# index, and its `body` is still byte-identical to the `"proposed"` one.
#
# That last paragraph is the whole point of the gap. `P6 CASE A` in
# `agent_compaction_test.exs` asserts reuse on the `replayed` boolean — a flag the reusing
# path writes ABOUT ITSELF — plus the ledger shape, and this build satisfies every one of
# those assertions. The fold is a pure function of `{run_id, turn_index, view state}`, so
# the body cannot tell a reuse from a re-derivation either. The only thing that can is what
# the replay SPENDS, and before `test/ai/agent_fold_reuse_cost_test.exs` shipped, NOTHING
# measured it.
#
# Flips the REUSE arm ONLY. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red mean
# what it says: the DERIVE COST control in the same file (no ledger row to reuse, so the
# same fold is legitimately derived through `apply_fold!/4`, which this patch does not
# touch) still passes — both before and after — so the red fails because the REPLAY billed,
# not because folds stopped billing, stopped being recorded, or stopped being reused.
#
# `fold_entry_tokens/2` is introduced in the same hunk rather than reading the entry inline:
# a fold-ledger entry is decoded JSON whose token fields are only guaranteed present on
# entries this build wrote, and an inline `entry["input_tokens"]` would make the sabotage
# crash on a legacy entry instead of BILLING — a crash proves nothing about the property.
# Touches agent.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_fold_reuse_cost_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: CF-17(b) REUSE COST: a replay that REUSES the :proposed fold ledger row SPENDS NOTHING for it
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
@@ -1562,13 +1562,28 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Agent do
             folds,
             views.turn_lens,
             views.pending
-          )
+          ),
+        # SABOTAGE (CF-17(b), ADR-048 §6 / ruling UXD-18): the REPLAY BILLS FOR THE FOLD IT
+        # CLAIMS TO REUSE. The `replayed` stamp above is still written, the body is still
+        # byte-identical and there is still exactly ONE ledger entry per turn index — so
+        # every assertion `P6 CASE A` makes still holds. What changed is the only thing
+        # that distinguishes reuse from re-derivation: the spend. The tokens billed at
+        # checkpoint 1 are charged to the tenant a SECOND time on every replay.
+        input_tokens_used: run.input_tokens_used + fold_entry_tokens(entry, "input_tokens"),
+        output_tokens_used: run.output_tokens_used + fold_entry_tokens(entry, "output_tokens")
       })
       |> Ash.update!(authorize?: false)
 
     {:ok, run, lines, views}
   end
 
+  defp fold_entry_tokens(entry, key) do
+    case Map.get(entry, key) do
+      n when is_integer(n) and n > 0 -> n
+      _ -> 0
+    end
+  end
+
